#: processes/kg/mount-dependency.bpmn:75
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Fetch the pinned tree (shallow, blobless). Read the harness's declaration from it; for each `needs` name, find that instance in the same tree, else follow a GITLINK at that tree as a pin into its own repository. A need found in neither is missing; one the downstream already holds is local. Paths and directories come from `mountDefaults` unless overridden."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/mount-dependency.bpmn:29
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Laying a harness — and every instance it needs — down from another repository at a pinned commit, as declared directories, with a lock that says exactly what arrived. You are in this process whenever a folio or harness needs a layer it does not hold: a downstream folio built on a content layer above this harness, a separated instance whose foundation lives elsewhere. The downstream names the harness, its repository and a 40-character pin as a `source.remote` instance in its root `index.config.json` (legacy: `remoteMounts` on its declaration, never both); everything else is read from the harness's own declaration at that pin. Every instance reached ends in one of three states — mounted, missing, could-not-determine — and the third is never reported as the first. The skill is `remote-mount`."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/mount-dependency.bpmn:45
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Mechanical from the declaration on: the same declaration mounts the same bytes in every container, and only an override by id changes where or what."
msgstr ""

