#: processes/kg/mount-dependency.bpmn:86
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Sparse checkout of the declaration and the chosen directories, copied to the mount path (by default the instance's home path, so relative imports and sibling discovery hold). Never onto tracked bytes; never onto a directory no lock says this mount made; never over edits to a previous mount — those are left untouched and reported. A replay of the lock tries the index's layers cache ref first (`refs/cat/layers/<key>`, then `refs/cat/layers/main`): one shallow fetch, every byte verified against the lock, and any layer that does not verify is fetched from its own repository."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/mount-dependency.bpmn:141
#. Diagram label
msgid "The closure is on disk, pinned and locked"
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/mount-dependency.bpmn:115
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "When the lock changed, the layers an agent's skills and memory are generated from changed with it. `mount:remote` re-runs the generators of what an agent actually reads — `skill:commands` (`.claude/commands/`) and `agent-memory` (`.claude/agent-memory/` and the `.agents/` copies) — from the checkout root, and a generator that fails fails the run. A re-pin commit therefore carries the new layers AND the surface rendered from them, because new layers shipped without their rendered surface fail the agent-memory tests."
msgstr ""

